a:["$","p","11",{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-300 leading-[1.85] mb-5","children":"This is where most self-appraisals collapse into a list of activities. Resist the urge to recap your sprint board. Pick two or three decisions you made that a peer could not or did not make, and describe them in active voice."}]
b:["$","h3","12",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-white mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-20","children":"R — Result: the number, plus the second-order effect"}]
c:["$","p","13",{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-300 leading-[1.85] mb-5","children":"A result without a number is an opinion. After the number, add one line of second-order impact — what changed downstream because of your result. This is the line that gets quoted in calibration."}]
d:["$","h2","14",{"id":"full-example","className":"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 scroll-mt-20","children":"A full STAR response, annotated"}]
e:["$","blockquote","15",{"className":"border-l-4 border-indigo-500/60 bg-indigo-500/5 pl-5 py-4 my-6 rounded-r-xl","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-200 italic leading-relaxed","children":["“","Q4 dashboard load times had degraded from 1.2s to 4.8s after the analytics migration, and three enterprise accounts had cited it in renewal conversations [S]. I was asked to lead the recovery work and own the new performance budget [T]. I profiled the query path, identified an unindexed join in the metrics rollup, and partnered with the data team to add a covering index plus a Redis-backed read path for the hottest 12 queries [A]. P75 load time dropped from 4.8s to 1.5s within two weeks, all three at-risk renewals closed on time, and the Redis pattern has since been adopted by two other product surfaces [R].","”"]}],["$","footer",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-xs font-mono text-indigo-400/80 uppercase tracking-wider","children":["— ","Senior Software Engineer STAR example"]}]]}]
f:["$","h2","16",{"id":"common-mistakes","className":"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 scroll-mt-20","children":"Five common STAR mistakes that cost promotions"}]
10:["$","ol","17",{"className":"space-y-2 mb-6 pl-5 list-decimal text-gray-300 text-[15px] leading-[1.85] marker:text-indigo-400","children":[["$","li","0",{"children":"Burying the result. The Result line should arrive before the reader loses interest — first 60 words, not the last sentence of a paragraph."}],["$","li","1",{"children":"Claiming team outcomes as personal ones. \"We shipped X\" reads as deflection. Pick the slice that was yours."}],["$","li","2",{"children":"Stacking vague verbs. \"Drove,\" \"led,\" \"managed\" without a concrete decision underneath is filler."}],["$","li","3",{"children":"Skipping the second-order effect. A single number can look anomalous. The second-order line proves it was real."}],["$","li","4",{"children":"Writing in past-perfect mush (\"had been working on,\" \"would often\") instead of clean past-tense action."}]]}]
11:["$","h2","18",{"id":"mapping-to-okrs","className":"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 scroll-mt-20","children":"Mapping STAR to your company's review criteria"}]
12:["$","p","19",{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-300 leading-[1.85] mb-5","children":"Most performance frameworks score on three to five competencies — typically Execution, Collaboration, Technical Excellence, and Leadership. A complete self-appraisal pairs one or two STAR responses to each competency. If you cannot map a STAR response to a named competency, it likely belongs in a separate \"context\" section instead of the formal review."}]
13:["$","aside","20",{"className":"my-7 p-5 rounded-2xl border bg-indigo-500/5 border-indigo-500/20","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold mb-2 text-indigo-300","children":"Tip: write STAR responses weekly, not yearly"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed","children":"The single biggest reason self-appraisals are weak is recency bias — you remember the last six weeks and forget the rest of the year. A five-minute weekly log captured throughout the year produces dramatically better STAR responses at review time, because you still remember the numbers."}]]}]
14:["$","h2","21",{"id":"how-impactly-helps","className":"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 scroll-mt-20","children":"How Impactly AI turns weekly logs into STAR responses"}]
15:["$","p","22",{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-300 leading-[1.85] mb-5","children":"Impactly AI is built for exactly this workflow. You log five minutes per week — what shipped, what was hard, what you learned. At review time, the appraisal engine groups your entries by competency, drafts STAR-formatted responses against your company's OKRs and core values, and lets you customize the tone (assertive, collaborative, or leadership-focused). Everything stays in your private workspace, encrypted, with no LLM training on your data."}]
16:["$","div","23",{"className":"my-8 p-6 glass rounded-2xl border border-indigo-500/20 text-center","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm md:text-base text-gray-200 mb-4","children":"Try the appraisal generator on a free account — no credit card, Google or GitHub login."}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://app.impactlyai.com/login","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-500 to-purple-500 hover:from-indigo-600 hover:to-purple-600 text-white font-bold text-sm rounded-xl","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Generate My First STAR Appraisal"}],["$","$L3",null,{"iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M5 12h14","key":"1ays0h"}],["path",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7","key":"xquz4c"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-right w-4 h-4"}]]}]]}]
17:["$","h2","24",{"id":"faqs","className":"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 scroll-mt-20","children":"FAQs about the STAR method"}]
18:["$","h3","25",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-white mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-20","children":"Is STAR overkill for a junior-level review?"}]
19:["$","p","26",{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-300 leading-[1.85] mb-5","children":"No. Junior-level calibration committees still need to see specificity, and STAR forces you to put numbers next to your work — which is the exact gap committees flag for engineers who are otherwise ready for promotion."}]
1a:["$","h3","27",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-white mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-20","children":"What if I do not have hard numbers for an accomplishment?"}]
1b:["$","p","28",{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-300 leading-[1.85] mb-5","children":"Use proxy metrics: cycle time, code review turnaround, support tickets deflected, design-review approvals first-pass, customer interview count. Any countable proxy beats a verb-only Result line."}]
1c:["$","h3","29",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-white mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-20","children":"Can I use STAR in mid-year check-ins, or is it only for annual reviews?"}]
1d:["$","p","30",{"className":"text-[15px] md:text-base text-gray-300 leading-[1.85] mb-5","children":"STAR is appropriate any time the audience is making a calibration or promotion decision. For weekly 1:1s, simpler bullet-point logs are usually faster — and those bullets become the raw material for the STAR responses you write at review time."}]
20:null
